          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On December 25, 2011, between 6:35 and 6:40 PM, a motorist and his passenger observed in the sky a bright, stationary light performing swinging movements. Initially thinking it was a firework, the witness continued driving but then stopped to take photographs. Upon arriving home, they noticed three luminescent masses of color in a line, gaining altitude. The objects disappeared very quickly. No noise was heard during the several-minute observation. No other testimony about this phenomenon was collected by the gendarmerie. The hypothesis of Thai lanterns remains the most probable; it is consistent with the wind and the photographs, and is highly plausible for the observation date. However, it should be noted that the irregular movement of the lanterns raises questions: one would have to assume the hypothesis of upward currents along the path. This case is classified as \"B\": probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "0f3325aeb48669e1a1ea8cb737f946ae8133d298e1616c7362c927e16bf612fd"
        }
